  "body": "Clamp oversized suffix ranges for nonempty blob URLs\n\nFor a 10-byte Blob, `Range: bytes=-12` currently produces a start of −2 and an end of 9. Blob slicing then returns only two bytes with `Content-Range: bytes -2-9/10`.\n\nClamp an oversized suffix to the nonempty Blob’s size before subtraction, matching RFC 9110 §14.1.2. The result is all ten bytes and `Content-Range: bytes 0-9/10`. Empty-Blob and zero-suffix behavior is unchanged.\n\nValidation: checked 28 size/suffix combinations. Local Bikeshed generation succeeded with an offline data-update warning. A corresponding WPT oversized-suffix test is still needed; no browser interoperability or implementer approval is claimed.\n\n- [ ] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed).\n- [ ] WPT tests are written and available for review.\n- [ ] Implementation bugs are filed.\n- [ ] An MDN issue is filed.\n- [x] This comment includes a clear commit message.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/fetch/1967.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 10, 2026, 1:53 AM UTC (6a2a9a6)\">Preview</a> | <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/fetch/1967/59afe34...6a2a9a6.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 10, 2026, 1:53 AM UTC (6a2a9a6)\">Diff</a>",
